For each number in the array, we create a variable `isPrime` initialized to `true`, since we assume all numbers pass initial checks.

We then loop through integers from 2 up to (but excluding) the current number being checked, making sure to exit the loop early once a non-prime factor is discovered (`break`). 

If at the end of the loop, none of those factors were successful in dividing the number evenly, then we consider it a prime.

Finally, we log the prime number (as long as its `isPrime` flag was still set at `true`) to the console. 

Note that this function assumes you only want to check if any of the numbers in the array are prime; if you also wanted to identify the first prime number encountered or the entire list of prime numbers, adjustments may be required.user

